{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/191428-ratkin-conversions","id":191428,"title":"Ratkin Conversions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-08T08:54:18-07:00","id":191428,"title":"Ratkin Conversions","content":"Not sure what to say about this. I was trying to build the old splats of changing breeds into something that'd balance well against werewolves. Never liked the idea that Uratha were the stars, really. What makes wolf more important than the rest of the gang, no? Yeah, there was the Changing Breeds supplement, but the rules in that thing were kinda broken, while the text was pretentious and condescending at times. I always thought War Against the Pure did it better.<br /> <br /> In short, I never finished this, but with the Idigam Chronicles coming out soon, I thought I'd at least share it before the rules became outdated. Let me know if you guys see anything interesting. I'm always up for feedback.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">----<br /> Rats. Few other mammals can be counted as being more prolific in both folklore, and sheer numbers. To some, they are a pestilence, bringing diseases such as the Black Plague across entire continents as they consume whatever they can find. To others, they are symbols of luck and good fortune, seemingly blessed by the gods as they survive the most extreme of changes in territory. Indeed, if a rat senses danger, they will quickly flee; a sign of warning to those who know what to look for.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Scavengers and survivors par excellence, the Little-folk have suffered the predations of many throughout the ages. ****</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Appearance and Forms:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Ratkin are made, not born. Even if the progeny of a wererat, a given mortal will only ever become a fellow wormtail if subjected to the Birthing Plague. Because of this, they only have 3 forms: human, hybrid, and beast.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The traits for hybrid form are Strength +1, Dexterity +4, Stamina +1, Size +1, a +2 to Perception checks, and Armor 1/1.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The traits for the ratkin\u2019s beast form are Dexterity +3, Size -4 (to minimum of 1) but only suffers a -1 to total number of Health boxes owned, and a +3 to Perception checks.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Reproduction:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Every member of the nest was born from enduring what\u2019s called the Birthing Plague. Once every ten years (minus levels in Primal Urge), a ratkin must spend 1 point of Willpower to infect a mortal with his supernatural illness. This is done in a number of ways. Perhaps by making direct contact with the target\u2019s flesh, or having said-target inhale his breath, or ingest something the ratkin already made contact with. Sure enough, within an incubation period of one week, illness befalls the mortal. This disease does not spread, nor is it possible to cure with treatment. In short, the victim suffers from mostly random symptoms, some of which can be fatal. During its course, the sickness causes a bizarre state of manic hallucination, most survivors remembering the sound of many voices being present. Believed to be the spirits of past ratkin, these voices counsel the newcomer, each trying to sway them towards an Auspice within the colony.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Upon deciding (or succumbing to infection), the voices dissipate from the target, along with the ailments suffered during the Plague. If the former, then the subject will fully become ratkin; acquiring innate knowledge on how to shift between forms and back. Everything else must be learned the old fashioned way, though usually fellow ratkin will appear to greet and explain the situation.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Character Creation:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Inborn Aspects: Shapeshifting, Regeneration, Shadowborn</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Common Aspects: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Rage: Madness Rage (Mania)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Territories: ***</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Concepts: ***</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspices</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Unlike werewolves, the Ratkin choose their auspice during the hallucinations of the Birthing Plague. Usually, such choices are made in the spur of the moment rather than well thought out, and since this choice is always final, a wererat can find himself easily screwed over. Regardless, every worm-tail gains a boon that will often aid him with their sacred duty to the nest.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Tunnel Runners -- The messengers, scouts, and spies of Ratkin society, they know a lot about how to get around safely and without notice.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Shadow Seers -- Mystics with secret knowledge and special insight into the mysteries of the Shadow, but have trouble remaining rooted in the physical world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Knife-Skulkers -- Enforcers, assassins, and the keepers of peace within the warrens. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Warriors (Blade Slaves) -- Protectors, soldiers, and armed to the teeth against enemies of all kinds. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Engineers -- Tinkerers, workers, and craftsmen of the warrens.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">---</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Munchmausen --</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Plague Lords -- Traitors in service to the Beshilu.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Twitchers -- Crazy ass motherfuckers</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Auspices Indepth</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Tunnel Runners</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The scouts and spies of the nest, the Tunnel Runners are often the ones with the most connections above and under the city limits. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pending...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary Renown: Purity</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Specialty Skills: Athletics, Stealth, Streetwise</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gift Lists: Grotto, Evasion, Stealth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Ability: Wandering Visions. If the Tunnel Runner ever becomes lost, he can potentially gain a vision from Mother Rat of where he needs to go, and in which direction it is. Note that this vision isn't prophetic, nor does it necessarily guide him to where he wants to go, but rather, where he needs to go.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Change:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Quote:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Shadow Seers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pending...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary Renown: Wisdom</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Specialty Skills: Investigation, Occult, Persuasion</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gift Lists: Death, Insight, Warding</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Ability: Spirit Sight. The seer may roll Wits + Occult + Wisdom to peer across the Gauntlet, success meaning she understand what is happening on both sides of it without penalty. This ability lasts for one scene. It works with only one of the character's senses, which is chosen upon activating, and if used again during the same scene, resets both time and choice.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Change:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Quote:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Knife Skulkers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pending...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary Renown: Honor</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Specialty Skills: Empathy, Politics, Stealth</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gift Lists: Alpha, Retribution, Stalking</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Ability: Assassin's Creed. A Knife Skulker gains the 9-again rule on all stealth-checks when attempting to kill a wormtail who has broken the laws of his nest, or a target whom he knows to have shed the blood of the innocent. This blessing goes away if the Knife Skulker willingly slays anyone to reach the target, or if they confront said-target face to face. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Change:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Quote:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Warriors</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pending...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary Renown: Glory</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Specialty Skills: Brawl, Intimidation, Weaponry</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gift Lists: Battle, Endurance, Inspiration </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Ability: Pain Dagger. Once per day, a warrior can imbue a bladed weapon with his own essence, making it capable of striking spirits and other ephemeral creatures. This effect lasts for a scene, and requires the warrior to coat the weapon in blood from a fresh wound. Note that the weapon has the potential to cause staggering amounts of pain regardless of damage given if the blade makes contact with the skin.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Change: A blade slave is often found in those who've suffered the ravages of combat. The visions they endure while under the Birthing Plague are cobbled together from memories of pain, anger, helplessness, and the desire to fight on. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Quote:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Engineers</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Pending...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Primary Renown: Cunning</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Specialty Skills: Craft, Larceny, Science</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Gift Lists: Shaping, Technology, Urban </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Auspice Ability: Clever Hands. An engineer gains +2 dice to checks centered around crafting, repairing, or sabotaging mundane machinery. This ability does not affect machines currently influenced by supernatural Gifts or a spirit's Numina.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">The Change:</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Quote:</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Ratkin Rites &amp; Rituals</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Rite of the Birthing Mother (\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In times of great duress, when numbers are few, and the nest is vulnerable, it becomes dangerous for ratkin to venture out and infect potential mortals with the Birthing Plague. Fortunately, most colonies have at least one ritualist who knows this rite, said to have been given by Mother Rat herself long ago. With it, a single willing female (either mortal or ratkin) can take on the sacred duty of Den Mother, creating the next generation of ratkin by channeling Mama Rat\u2019s ample fertility and love for her children. In doing so, she spares her packmates the need to spread infection, and becomes immune to rage whilst in Hybrid form and pregnant with her offspring.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Performing the Rite: Within a circle marked in blood or urine, the would-be Den Mother lies naked atop a bed of some kind (traditionally one made from straw or blankets, if possible). The ritualist then begins marking the woman\u2019s body with symbols of the Rat Mother, spending 1 point of essence per hour, all while asking the target to affirm her role and desire to serve the colony. Upon accepting, the ritemaster will guide the woman in a formal oath, that she will protect and nurture her young without hesitation, and propagate for the good of the nest.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Dice Pool: Harmony</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Action: Extended (12 successes; each roll represents 30 minutes of effort)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Roll Results</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Dramatic Failure: The rite appears to backfire, causing all ratkin associated with the nest to grow ever needing to spread the birthing plague to the point it\u2019s all they can think about till acted upon.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Failure: No successes accumulate</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Success: Successes accumulate. If the rite is finished, the subject becomes blessed by Mama Rat, becoming an avatar of fertility as her body swells in size by +1. In addition to members of the local nest no longer being instinctively compelled to spread their numbers, the Den Mother does not suffer from Rage when in Hybrid form so long as she is pregnant. Note that after becoming a Den Mother, the subject is highly susceptible to seduction, remaining \u201cin heat\u201d till impregnated by either a fellow ratkin, or mortal. Such pregnancies last for 5 months as opposed to the normal 9. Often, the Den Mother will be forced to shift into Hybrid form as she gives birth, with the average litter being 3 to 6. Each child has the shapechanging ability at birth, not needing to undergo the First Change as the Forsaken do. However, such children have a shorter lifespan than most, usually dying around the age of 40. They also suffer from a mild version of the Rapture till they reach adolescence, when it becomes full-blown.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"> Exceptional Success: Successes accumulate. Gaining 17+ successes by the end of the rite means the Den Mother resonates with Mother Rat\u2019s love that for any of her kin to strike at her requires them spending 1 point of Willpower. She also gains a +2 to all social rolls involving the colony.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Rite of the Rat King (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Despite the singular name, a &quot;Rat King&quot; is comprised of at least 3 wormtails (traditionally elders) combining their essence, knowledge, and wisdom into a single avatar. Through this spiritual gestalt, a given colony of rats (now called a kingdom) acquires a powerful guardian with which to stand behind in times of peace and war alike.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">In truth, the Rat King is not always male, or even of one gender. Taking on both the physical and mental characteristics of those participating (now known as the King's Court), the Rat King can appear hermaphroditic if a wormtail of the opposite gender is involved. However, this generally holds little problem, as the rite endows the King with an air of regal authority. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It is uncertain whether the Rat King is controlled by the Court, or of independent mind, as once the Court is dismissed the participants rarely remember the exact details of their shared experience. What is known is that the Rat King knows who and what he is, having all the memories and skills of his creators. Mechanically speaking, he takes the highest ranking stat level among the court, eg; if one of the participants had Strength 4, and the others had either equal or less dots in that attribute, the Rat King would have Strength 4. This also counts with skills, Primal Urge, and Renown. Note that the Rat King also knows whatever Gifts were known by the Court, and also acquires both the physical and mental merits of said-Court (which do not stack). He maintains the template of a fellow ratkin, able to shift between human, hybrid, and beast form. He retains the limitation of having only 7 dots worth of Aspects, which must be chosen from those the Court already has (any dots remaining are rendered null). The Rat King's starting essence is determined by the number of participants in the rite. One problem that is always evident within a Rat King is suffers whatever derangements the Court may have, and has a Harmony level equal to the lowest among Court members. Finally, any damage dealt to the Rat King is also felt by the Court, who each suffer equal levels of bashing (regardless of lethal or aggravated). If a rite participant should die during the Rat King's reign, whatever advantages he or she offered disappear. And though the Rat king need not eat or drink, the Court surely does, meaning someone must tend to them, lest they starve and die. To dispel the rite, one need only untie the tails of the Court, thus freeing them should the &quot;king&quot; prove himself a tyrant. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#2C3635\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Performing the Rite: The participating ratkin, all of which must be willing volunteers, must sit in a circle with their backs to each other. The Ritemaster (or a ritual aide) must then place within the center a bowl anointed with symbols of the first tongue, filled with a brew formed from pungent herbs, moss, and fungi. As the ritual progresses, each participant must expend 1 Essence, slowly transition from human to hybrid-form, their tails instinctively drawn into the bowl's liquid content. Some ritemasters provide mats for the ratkin to lay upon, their body's unable to move as their minds meld together. The rite is complete when all participants' tails have wrapped and coiled themselves around each other--the liquid evaporating to become the Rat King.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}